gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Core Geospatial Primitive Types",
  "labels": ["migration","core"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\nThe `AgOpenGPS.Core.Models` base namespace defines immutable geometric primitives as C# `struct`s: `GeoCoord` (northing/easting), `Wgs84` (WGS84 lat/lon with haversine distance), `GeoDelta` (2D vector with cross-product), `GeoDir` (heading angle in [0, 2π)), `GeoArea`, `GeoCircle` (arc-length for Dubins paths), `GeoLineSegment` (parametric intersection), `GeoBoundingBox` (mutable include/scale), `LocalPlane` (WGS84 ↔ flat projection via series approximation), and `XyCoord`/`XyDelta` for screen space. Operator overloads and `InvariantCulture` are used throughout. These are the load-bearing primitives for every guidance, field, and rendering computation.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoCoord.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/Wgs84.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoDelta.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoDir.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoArea.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoCircle.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoLineSegment.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoBoundingBox.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoCoordDir.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/LocalPlane.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/Units.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/XyCoord.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/XyDelta.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\n`GeoCoord` exposes `distance_squared`, `distance`, `min`, `max`, `average`, `triangle_area`, `quad_area`, plus `__add__`/`__sub__` with `GeoDelta`. `Wgs84` validates range, computes haversine distance and bearing-distance projection. `GeoDelta` provides `length_squared`, `length`, `cross_product_z`, scalar multiply. `GeoDir` wraps angle in [0, 2π) with `perpendicular_left`, `perpendicular_right`, `inverted`, and float add/subtract (normalised). `GeoCircle` computes `point_on_circle` and signed `arc_length` given `TurnType`. `GeoLineSegment` holds two `GeoCoord` endpoints and computes parametric `intersection_point`. `GeoBoundingBox` is mutable: `include(coord/bb)`, `is_inside`, `scaled`. `LocalPlane` exposes `convert_wgs84_to_geo_coord` and inverse using series approximation. `TurnType` enum (`Straight`, `Left`, `Right`) belongs here.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- Each type becomes a Python `dataclass` (frozen for immutable types, regular for `GeoBoundingBox`).\n- Full dunder methods: `__add__`, `__sub__`, `__mul__`, `__neg__`, `__eq__` on relevant types.\n- Pure Python `float` (64-bit); no `numpy` dependency in this module.\n- `GeoDir` angle normalisation must keep value in [0, 2π).\n- `TurnType` as `enum.Enum`.\n- Full type hints throughout.\n- `Units` (degrees↔radians) extracted to `agopengps/core/models/base/units.py`.\n- `GeoBoundingBox.create_empty()` as a `classmethod`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All thirteen types implemented with correct behaviour matching C# counterparts.\n- [ ] `GeoCoord.distance(coord2)` matches C# result to floating-point precision.\n- [ ] `Wgs84.distance_in_meters` haversine result matches C# to within 1 mm over 20 000 km.\n- [ ] `LocalPlane` round-trip (WGS84 → GeoCoord → WGS84) error < 1 cm at 55° latitude.\n- [ ] `GeoLineSegment.intersection_point` returns `None` for parallel segments.\n- [ ] `GeoBoundingBox` correctly unfrozen/mutable.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests covering all cases in `AgOpenGPS.Core.Tests/Models/Base/`.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting and formatting checks.\n\n## Dependencies\n- None — foundational module; all other issues depend on this one.\n\n## Notes\n- C# struct → Python frozen dataclass for immutable types; return new instances, do not mutate.\n- `LocalPlane` uses a series approximation — do not replace with `geopy`. Numeric agreement with existing tests is required.\n- `GeoBoundingBox.CreateEmpty()` (C# static factory) → `classmethod` in Python."
}'
