gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Field Domain Models (Field, Boundary, Contour, Flag, TramLines, WorkedArea)",
  "labels": ["migration","core","data"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\nThe `AgOpenGPS.Core.Models.Field` namespace defines the in-memory domain model for an agricultural field. `Field` is the aggregate root: it holds a `DirectoryInfo` reference and optional `BingMap`, `Boundary`, `Contour`, `FieldOverview`, `List<Flag>`, `List<HeadPath>`, `RecordedPath`, `TramLines`, and `WorkedArea`. `Boundary` contains an outer `BoundaryPolygon` and a list of inner boundaries (holes). `BoundaryPolygon` wraps a `GeoPolygon` with area computation. `WorkedArea` tracks covered area for section mapping. `TramLines` stores tramline offsets. `RecordedPath`/`RecordedPoint` capture driven paths with heading. All field components are nullable/optional (a freshly created field may have none of them). `FieldDescription`/`FieldOverview` provide lightweight summary data for listing. `SharedFieldProperties` holds a drift-compensation `GeoDelta` shared across all field operations.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/Field.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/Boundary.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/BoundaryPolygon.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/Contour.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/FieldDescription.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/FieldGrid.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/FieldOverview.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/Fields.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/Flag.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/HeadPath.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/QuadStrip.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/RecordedPath.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/RecordedPoint.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/SharedFieldProperties.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/TramLines.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/TramModes.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/WorkedArea.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Field/BingMap.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nAll eighteen classes must be converted. `Field` becomes a Python dataclass or plain class whose path is a `pathlib.Path`. All sub-models (`BingMap`, `Boundary`, `Contour`, etc.) are optional (default `None`). `Boundary` holds an optional `outer_boundary: BoundaryPolygon` and `inner_boundaries: list[BoundaryPolygon]`; its `area` property delegates to the outer. `Fields` acts as a collection (enumerate, select active, delete by path). `SharedFieldProperties` holds a `GeoDelta` drift compensation. `TramModes` is an enum. `RecordedPoint` pairs a `GeoCoord` with a `GeoDir` heading. `FieldDescription` provides a lightweight summary (name, area, GPS bounding box) for UI list views. `WorkedArea` tracks a list of `QuadStrip`s representing covered swaths.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- Use `@dataclass` for all model types; use `field(default_factory=list)` for list members.\n- `Field.name` property derives from `path.name`.\n- All optional associations typed as `T | None` with default `None`.\n- `Fields` exposes `active_field`, `select_field(path)`, `delete_field(path)`, `enumerate_fields()` using `pathlib.Path`.\n- `TramModes` as `enum.Enum`.\n- No ORM or database — fields are directory-backed (file persistence is handled in a separate streamer issue).\n- Full type hints; `from __future__ import annotations` at top of each file.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All model classes implemented with correct attribute names and types.\n- [ ] `Boundary.area` delegates to `outer_boundary.area` and returns `0.0` when `outer_boundary` is `None`.\n- [ ] `Fields.delete_field(path)` removes the entry from the in-memory collection and the filesystem directory.\n- [ ] `Field` can be constructed with only a `path` argument; all other fields are `None`.\n- [ ] All public members have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest unit tests for construction, optionality, and area delegation.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting and formatting checks.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Core Geospatial Primitive Types) — uses `GeoCoord`, `GeoDir`, `GeoPolygon`, `GeoDelta`.\n\n## Notes\n- C# uses `DirectoryInfo` for file system references; Python uses `pathlib.Path`.\n- `BingMap` stores tile metadata and a bounding box — no bitmap loading in this model (that is for the rendering layer)."
}'
