gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] GeoPath and GeoPolygon Collection Types",
  "labels": ["migration","core"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\nThe `GeoPaths` and `GeoPolygons` subdirectories define ordered collections of `GeoCoord` points. `GeoPathBase` is the abstract base providing index access and count. `GeoPath` is a plain ordered list of `GeoCoord`s. `GeoPathWithHeading` extends this with a parallel `GeoDir` array so each point has an associated heading. `GeoPolygon` is a closed `GeoPath` with an `area` property computed using the shoelace formula (via `GeoCoord.TriangleArea`). `GeoPolygonWithHeading` adds the heading array. These types are used pervasively: boundary rings, contour lines, recorded paths, tramlines, and Dubins path waypoints all use them.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoPaths/GeoPathBase.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoPaths/GeoPath.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoPaths/GeoPathWithHeading.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoPolygons/GeoPolygon.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Base/GeoPolygons/GeoPolygonWithHeading.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\n`GeoPathBase` → abstract Python base class with `__len__`, `__getitem__`, and `count` property. `GeoPath` → concrete list-backed class with `add(coord)`, `clear()`, iteration support. `GeoPathWithHeading` → pairs `list[GeoCoord]` with `list[GeoDir]`; `get_heading(i)` retrieves the heading at index `i`; `add(coord, heading)` appends both simultaneously. `GeoPolygon` → subclass of `GeoPath`; `area` property sums triangle areas via shoelace. `GeoPolygonWithHeading` → subclass of `GeoPathWithHeading` with same `area` property.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- Abstract base using `abc.ABC` with `@abstractmethod` for index access.\n- `GeoPath` backed by `list[GeoCoord]` (not `numpy` array in this module).\n- `GeoPathWithHeading` must keep heading list in sync with coord list — raise `IndexError` if lengths diverge.\n- `GeoPolygon.area` computes the shoelace sum using `GeoCoord.triangle_area`.\n- Support `for coord in path:` iteration via `__iter__`.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `GeoPath` and `GeoPathWithHeading` iteration and index access work correctly.\n- [ ] `GeoPolygon.area` matches the C# shoelace computation for known polygons.\n- [ ] Adding a coord to `GeoPathWithHeading` without a heading raises `TypeError`.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests for construction, area, and iteration.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Core Geospatial Primitive Types).\n\n## Notes\n- These are used as data containers everywhere in the system — keep construction API simple.\n- The C# implementations expose `Count` (Python: `__len__`) and indexer `[i]` (Python: `__getitem__`)."
}'
