gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Field File Streamers — Serialise/Deserialise Field Data",
  "labels": ["migration","core","data"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\nThe `AgOpenGPS.Core.Streamers.Field` namespace implements field persistence. `FieldStreamer` is the façade: it orchestrates ten sub-streamers (`BingMapStreamer`, `BoundaryStreamer`, `ContourStreamer`, `FlagListStreamer`, `RecordedPathStreamer`, `TramLinesStreamer`, `WorkAreaStreamer`, `FieldDescriptionStreamer`, `FieldAspectStreamer`, `OverviewStreamer`, `PerformanceReportStreamer`). `GeoStreamWriter` extends `StreamWriter` with typed `Write*` helpers (`WriteGeoCoordEN`, `WriteWgs84`, `WriteGeoPath`, `WriteGeoPolygon`, etc.), all using `InvariantCulture`. `GeoStreamReader` mirrors it for reading. Each sub-streamer reads/writes a named text file in the field directory (e.g., `Boundary.txt`, `ContourStore.txt`). All files use `$` header lines for format detection. The streamer layer is injected with an `IFieldStreamerPresenter` to report errors without throwing.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/FieldStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/GeoStreamWriter.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/GeoStreamReader.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/BoundaryStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/ContourStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/FlagListStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/RecordedPathStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/TramLinesStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/WorkAreaStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/BingMapStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/FieldDescriptionStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/OverviewStreamer.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Streamers/Field/PerformanceReportStreamer.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\n`GeoStreamWriter` → a context-manager class wrapping a `pathlib.Path`; methods write typed lines to a `TextIOWrapper` with `locale.setlocale` or explicit `float.__format__`. `GeoStreamReader` → counterpart for reading, parsing invariant-culture floats, booleans, and lists. Each sub-streamer exposes `read(field_dir: Path) -> T | None` and `write(data: T, field_dir: Path) -> None`. `FieldStreamer` composes all sub-streamers and provides a high-level API: `read_boundary(field)`, `write_boundary(field)`, `read_contour(field)`, etc. Error reporting calls into an injected callback rather than raising.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `GeoStreamWriter` and `GeoStreamReader` as context managers (`__enter__`/`__exit__`).\n- All floating-point I/O uses `locale`-independent formatting (`f\"{value:.7f}\"` or similar).\n- Each sub-streamer is a standalone class or module with `read` and `write` functions.\n- `FieldStreamer` injected with an `on_error: Callable[[str], None]` instead of a presenter interface.\n- `pathlib.Path` used exclusively for file operations.\n- Atomic writes: write to `.tmp` then rename, matching C# pattern.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `GeoStreamWriter` writes `GeoCoord`, `Wgs84`, `GeoPath`, `GeoPolygon` in format readable by `GeoStreamReader`.\n- [ ] `BoundaryStreamer.read` correctly parses both legacy (duplicate flag) and normal boundary files.\n- [ ] `FieldStreamer.read_boundary(field)` sets `field.boundary` from disk.\n- [ ] Atomic write behaviour: if write fails partway, original file is not corrupted.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests using tmp_path fixture for read/write round-trips.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives), Issue #2 (Field Models), Issue #3 (GeoPath/GeoPolygon).\n\n## Notes\n- `InvariantCulture` in C# → Python requires explicit format strings or `locale.setlocale(LC_NUMERIC, \"C\")`.\n- `AppendUnsavedWork` for `Contour` and `WorkedArea` appends a partial update without rewriting the entire file — preserve this optimisation."
}'
