gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] AgShare HTTP API Client (AgShareClient, AgShareResult, DTOs)",
  "labels": ["migration","api"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`AgShareClient` in `AgOpenGPS.Core.AgShare` is an async HTTP client that communicates with the AgShare field-sharing web service using API-key authentication. It exposes `check_api_async` (static, validates connectivity), `upload_field_async` (HTTP PUT with JSON body), `get_own_fields_async` (GET list), `download_field_async` (GET by GUID), and `get_public_fields_async` (GET with lat/lon/radius, currently unimplemented). `AgShareResult`/`AgShareResult<T>` is a result-monad pattern: `is_successful`, `data` (generic), and `error` (typed `AgShareError`). `AgShareError` captures HTTP status codes, `HttpRequestException`, and `JsonException`. The DTOs (`CoordinateDto`, `GetFieldDto`, `GetOwnFieldDto`, `GuidanceTrackDto`, `PolygonDto`, `UploadFieldDto`) carry field geometry as arrays of lat/lon pairs. The client uses `Newtonsoft.Json` for serialisation and a 5-second timeout.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/AgShareClient.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/AgShareResult.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/AgShareError.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/AgShareHelper.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/Models/CoordinateDto.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/Models/GetFieldDto.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/Models/GetOwnFieldDto.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/Models/GuidanceTrackDto.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/Models/PolygonDto.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/AgShare/Models/UploadFieldDto.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\n`AgShareClient` → Python class using `httpx.AsyncClient` with `Authorization: ApiKey <key>` header and a 5-second timeout. All methods `async`. `check_api` is a static `async` method that creates a temporary client. `AgShareResult` / `AgShareResult[T]` → Python `dataclass` or typed `Result` pattern using a `dataclasses.dataclass` with `is_successful: bool`, `data: T | None`, `error: AgShareError | None`. All DTOs → Pydantic `BaseModel` for automatic JSON deserialisation and validation.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `httpx.AsyncClient` for async HTTP; `asyncio.timeout` or `httpx` timeout parameter for 5-second limit.\n- All DTOs as Pydantic `BaseModel` with snake_case aliases for JSON fields.\n- `AgShareResult[T]` uses Python generics (`Generic[T]`).\n- `AgShareError` captures `error_type: Literal[\"invalid_api_key\", \"wrong_status_code\", \"http_error\", \"json_error\"]` plus message.\n- `AgShareClient.update_settings` recreates the internal client with new URL and key.\n- `get_public_fields_async` must raise `NotImplementedError` matching the C# TODO comment.\n- Full type hints; `asyncio` compatible.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `check_api_async` returns `AgShareResult` with `is_successful=True` on HTTP 200.\n- [ ] `check_api_async` returns `AgShareResult` with `error.error_type=\"invalid_api_key\"` on HTTP 401.\n- [ ] `upload_field_async` serialises `UploadFieldDto` and issues HTTP PUT.\n- [ ] `get_own_fields_async` deserialises JSON response into `list[GetOwnFieldDto]`.\n- [ ] `download_field_async` deserialises JSON response into `GetFieldDto`.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests using `respx` or `pytest-httpx` to mock HTTP responses.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives — Wgs84 used in DTOs indirectly).\n\n## Notes\n- Replace `Newtonsoft.Json` with Pydantic v2 for DTO deserialisation.\n- `httpx` is preferred over `aiohttp` for consistency with modern Python async patterns.\n- The `get_public_fields_async` method is unimplemented in C# — keep it as `NotImplementedError` in Python too, with a TODO comment."
}'
