gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] XML Settings Handler (AgLibrary.Settings.XmlSettingsHandler)",
  "labels": ["migration","config"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`XmlSettingsHandler` in `AgLibrary` is a reflection-based XML settings serialiser/deserialiser. `LoadXMLFile` reads a hand-crafted XML format (root: `configuration/userSettings/<ClassName>/<setting name=... serializeAs=...>/<value>`) using `XmlTextReader`, mapping XML attribute `name` to public fields on the target object via `FieldInfo.SetValue`. It handles `string`, `enum`, primitives (`int`, `double`, `bool`, etc.), `Color`, `Point`, `Size`, generic `List<T>`, `T[]`, and arbitrary serialisable classes via `XmlSerializer`. `SaveXMLFile` mirrors this using `XmlTextWriter` with `Indentation=4`. Atomic write (`.tmp` + rename) is used. Error handling swallows exceptions in release mode and re-throws in debug. `LoadResult` enum signals `Ok`, `MissingFile`, or `Failed`.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgLibrary/Settings/XmlSettingsHandler.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\n`XmlSettingsHandler.load_xml_file(file_path, obj)` → reads the XML and uses `setattr` (not `FieldInfo`) to apply values to the target Python object; must handle `str`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `Enum`, `list`, and nested objects. `save_xml_file(file_path, obj)` → writes all public instance attributes in the same XML structure. `LoadResult` → Python `enum.Enum`. Atomic write using `pathlib.Path` with `.tmp` rename. No `System.Drawing.Color`/`Point`/`Size` — these Windows types must be replaced with simple tuples or dataclasses.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- Use Python `xml.etree.ElementTree` (stdlib) for parsing and writing — no third-party XML library needed.\n- Reflection via `vars(obj)` / `getattr` / `setattr`.\n- Type coercion: detect target attribute type from type annotations (`__annotations__`) or current value type.\n- `Color`, `Point`, `Size` replaced with `tuple[int, int, int]`, `tuple[int, int]`, `tuple[int, int]` respectively.\n- Atomic write: write to `<path>.tmp`, then `Path.rename`.\n- `LoadResult` as `enum.Enum` with `OK`, `MISSING_FILE`, `FAILED` members.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `load_xml_file` correctly loads all types tested in `AgLibrary.Tests/Settings/XmlSettingsHandlerTests.cs`.\n- [ ] `save_xml_file` + `load_xml_file` round-trip preserves all field values.\n- [ ] Missing file returns `LoadResult.MISSING_FILE`.\n- [ ] Invalid XML field returns `LoadResult.FAILED` (does not raise).\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests mirroring the existing C# test cases.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- None — standalone utility.\n\n## Notes\n- The C# code silently ignores unknown settings names (forward compatibility). Python should do the same.\n- Windows `Color`/`Point`/`Size` types must not appear in the Python output — replace with named tuples or dataclasses that are serialisable as comma-separated strings in the same XML format."
}'
