gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Structured Logging Module (AgLibrary.Logging.Log)",
  "labels": ["migration","config"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`Log` in `AgLibrary.Logging` is a static class with an in-memory `StringBuilder` (`sbEvents`) that accumulates timestamped log lines. `EventWriter(message)` appends `HH:MM:SS-> message\\r` to the buffer. `FileSaveSystemEvents()` flushes the buffer to a log file in append mode. `CheckLogSize(logFile, sizeLimit)` trims the log file to below `sizeLimit` bytes by skipping the oldest lines, keeping approximately 20% extra space. The design is synchronous, not thread-safe, and uses wall-clock time (no log levels, no structured logging). The log file path is set once via `CheckLogSize`.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgLibrary/Logging/Log.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nThe three public methods: `event_writer(message: str) -> None`, `file_save_system_events() -> None`, and `check_log_size(log_file: str | Path, size_limit: int) -> None`. The in-memory buffer must survive across calls. Log file rotation must trim the file to below `size_limit` bytes while preserving the most recent lines.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- Replace the static `StringBuilder` with a module-level `collections.deque` or Python `logging.Handler` subclass.\n- **Preferred approach:** implement as a custom `logging.Handler` that buffers records and flushes to file, integrating with Python standard `logging` module so the rest of the system can use `logging.getLogger()` naturally.\n- `check_log_size` becomes a standalone function that trims the log file to below `size_limit` bytes (strip oldest lines).\n- Log line format: `HH:MM:SS -> {message}` (match C# format).\n- Thread-safe buffer using `threading.Lock` or `queue.Queue`.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `event_writer` appends timestamped lines to the in-memory buffer.\n- [ ] `file_save_system_events` flushes buffer to file in append mode and clears the buffer.\n- [ ] `check_log_size` trims the log file so its size falls below `size_limit` bytes.\n- [ ] Module integrates with Python standard `logging` (messages also appear via `logging.getLogger`).\n- [ ] Thread-safe: concurrent calls to `event_writer` do not corrupt the buffer.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests for buffer, flush, and trim behaviour.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- None — standalone utility.\n\n## Notes\n- The C# implementation is not thread-safe. The Python replacement must be thread-safe since AgIO and GPS run concurrent network loops.\n- The 0.5 MB log size limit is a magic constant in C# — make it a configurable parameter with a sensible default."
}'
