gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] NMEA Sentence Parser (GPS/Classes/CNMEA.cs)",
  "labels": ["migration","core"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`CNMEA` in the GPS project parses incoming NMEA 0183 sentences from GPS hardware. It maintains the current fix as a `vec2` (easting/northing), plus `altitude`, `speed`, `vtgSpeed`, `headingTrueDual`, `headingTrue`, `hdop`, `age`, `fixQuality`, `satellitesTracked`. `DefineLocalPlane` creates the `LocalPlane` from the first valid GPS fix, setting the coordinate origin for the entire session. `AverageTheSpeed` applies exponential smoothing (0.75/0.25). The parser handles GGA (fix quality, satellites, altitude, HDOP), VTG (speed/heading), RMC, and dual-antenna heading sentences. The class holds a direct reference to the `FormGPS` main form.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CNMEA.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nAll NMEA sentence parsing logic must be converted: GGA, VTG, RMC, and dual-antenna heading sentences. The class must set up a `LocalPlane` from the first valid fix. The tight coupling to `FormGPS` must be broken — replace with a callback or observer pattern. `AverageTheSpeed` exponential smoothing must be preserved.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `NmeaParser` class in `agopengps/gps/nmea_parser.py` with no UI coupling.\n- `parse_sentence(sentence: str) -> NmeaFix | None` parses a single NMEA sentence and returns an updated state object.\n- `NmeaFix` as a Pydantic or frozen dataclass holding all parsed fields.\n- `LocalPlane` injection via constructor — do not create it internally.\n- `on_local_plane_defined: Callable[[LocalPlane], None]` callback for first-fix event.\n- Checksum validation for all sentences.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] GGA sentence parsed correctly: fix quality, satellites, altitude, HDOP, lat, lon.\n- [ ] VTG sentence parsed: speed and heading.\n- [ ] Dual-antenna heading sentence parsed.\n- [ ] Invalid checksum returns `None` without raising.\n- [ ] `on_local_plane_defined` called exactly once per session on first valid GGA fix.\n- [ ] `average_the_speed` applies 0.75/0.25 exponential smoothing.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests with sample NMEA sentences.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives — Wgs84, LocalPlane).\n\n## Notes\n- The C# class holds a `FormGPS` reference for accessing shared state — in Python, use dependency injection or a dataclass state container.\n- NMEA checksum is XOR of all bytes between `$` and `*`.\n- Consider `pynmea2` library for sentence parsing as a base, but ensure the heading/dual-antenna proprietary sentences are handled custom."
}'
