gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Vehicle State and IMU/AHRS Sensor Fusion (CVehicle, CAHRS)",
  "labels": ["migration","core"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`CVehicle` holds all vehicle configuration and dynamic autosteer state: antenna geometry (`antenna_height`, `antenna_pivot`, `antenna_offset`), wheelbase, track width, look-ahead parameters for pure-pursuit and Stanley controllers, integral gains, steer angle limits, dead-zone heading/delay, hydraulic lift look-ahead, and a `slow_speed_cutoff`. `CAHRS` holds IMU/AHRS state: heading, roll, pitch, yaw rate, roll-zero calibration, a filter value, IMU-GPS fusion weights (`forward_comp`, `reverse_comp`, `fusion_weight`), and flags for reverse mode, roll invert, dual-antenna auto-switch. Both classes initialise from `Properties.Settings.Default` and hold a `FormGPS` reference for side-effecting UI calls. `VehicleConfig` is the pure model for rendering (type, colour, opacity, dimensions).\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CVehicle.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CAHRS.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Vehicle/VehicleConfig.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/Vehicle/BrandEnums.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\n`CVehicle` as a Python class holding all dynamic vehicle state; remove `FormGPS` reference. `CAHRS` as a Python class for IMU state, remove `FormGPS` reference. `VehicleConfig` as a frozen dataclass. `VehicleType` and `BrandEnums` as `enum.Enum` types. All settings values injected via constructor parameters or a `VehicleSettings` dataclass rather than reading from `Properties.Settings.Default`.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `VehicleState` dataclass holding all mutable operational fields (look-ahead, integral, dead-zone counters).\n- `VehicleConfig` frozen dataclass (rendering configuration).\n- `AhrsState` dataclass for IMU readings (heading, roll, pitch, yaw rate, filter).\n- Settings injected at construction time from a configuration object (see Issue #7).\n- `VehicleType` and vehicle brand enums as `enum.Enum`.\n- No UI references (`FormGPS`) — use callbacks or events for state change notifications.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `VehicleState` holds all fields present in `CVehicle` with correct Python types.\n- [ ] `AhrsState` holds all fields present in `CAHRS`.\n- [ ] `VehicleConfig` is frozen/immutable.\n- [ ] All settings read from injected config, not from a global settings object.\n- [ ] All public members have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest unit tests for construction and field access.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives), Issue #2 (Field Models — VehicleConfig colour type).\n\n## Notes\n- `CVehicle` in C# also handles guidance drawing (calls `GLW.*`) — strip all rendering calls; rendering belongs in Issue #11 (Guidance Algorithms).\n- All `Properties.Settings.Default.*` reads must become constructor arguments or a settings dataclass."
