gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] AB-Line and Curve Guidance Algorithms (CABLine, CABCurve, CGuidance)",
  "labels": ["migration","core"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`CABLine` implements A-B line guidance: it maintains a reference line defined by two `vec3` points (A and B), computes the current cross-track error (XTE) of the vehicle pivot from the nearest line segment, and calculates the required steer angle using both Stanley and Pure Pursuit algorithms. It handles multi-track snapping (`howManyPathsAway`), heading-same-way detection, and line width/guide-line rendering. `CABCurve` extends this to curved guidance lines (spline-based tracks). `CGuidance` is used for curved recorded-path following: it finds the nearest segment by dual binary search, computes heading error, applies Stanley correction, and accumulates an integral term. Both classes hold direct `FormGPS` references and interleave guidance math with OpenGL rendering calls.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CABLine.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CABCurve.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CGuidance.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CTrack.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nAll guidance math must be extracted from the `FormGPS`-coupled class into pure-Python functions/classes. The Stanley controller formula, Pure Pursuit radius computation, integral accumulation, heading-same-way detection, XTE computation, and multi-track snapping must all be preserved. Rendering calls (`GLW.*`) must be entirely removed from the guidance layer.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `AbLineGuidance` class in `agopengps/gps/guidance/ab_line.py` holding current guidance state.\n- `AbCurveGuidance` class for curved tracks.\n- `PathGuidance` class for recorded-path following (replaces `CGuidance`).\n- Pure functions `compute_stanley_steer_angle(xte, heading_error, speed, gains)` and `compute_pure_pursuit_steer_angle(goal_point, pivot, wheelbase)` extracted and unit-testable.\n- `Track` dataclass (`name`, `heading`, `point_a`, `point_b`, `nudge`) replacing `CTrk`.\n- No UI or OpenGL dependencies.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Stanley steer angle formula matches C# for known XTE and heading error inputs.\n- [ ] Pure Pursuit radius formula matches C# for known look-ahead and lateral offset inputs.\n- [ ] Multi-track snapping (`how_many_paths_away`) computed correctly given current position and track spacing.\n- [ ] Heading-same-way flag set/cleared correctly when vehicle heading changes relative to track heading.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests for Stanley, Pure Pursuit, and XTE computations.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives), Issue #3 (GeoPath), Issue #10 (Vehicle State).\n\n## Notes\n- The integral term in both Stanley and Pure Pursuit must be resettable on mode change — design with explicit `reset()` method.\n- `CABLine.BuildCurrentABLineList` computes the virtual A-B endpoints at ±2000m along the heading — preserve this extension approach."
}'
