gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] U-Turn and Headland Turn Logic (CYouTurn, CTurn, CDubins)",
  "labels": ["migration","core"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`CYouTurn` manages the automated U-turn sequence at field headlands. It determines when a turn should be triggered (`is_you_turn_triggered`), whether to turn left or right (`is_turn_left`), how many rows to skip (`row_skips_width`), and the U-turn radius. It delegates path construction to one of three strategies: Dubins path (via `CDubins`), Pure Pursuit arc, or a straight-through pattern. The computed turn path is stored in `yt_list` as a list of `vec3` waypoints. During the turn, the vehicle follows this path using the same Pure Pursuit / Stanley algorithm as straight-line guidance. `CTurn` encapsulates headland turn geometry. `CDubins` wraps the six Dubins path types (LSL, RSR, RSL, LSR, RLR, LRL) and selects the shortest feasible one — this duplicates the logic in `AgOpenGPS.Core.Models.Guidance.DubinsPath` but with `vec3` types.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CYouTurn.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CTurn.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CTurnLines.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CDubins.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nAll U-turn trigger logic, turn-direction selection, row-skip computation, Dubins path waypoint generation, and headland path following must be converted. `CDubins` in the GPS project must be reconciled with the Core `DubinsPath` hierarchy (Issue #4) — use the Core implementation rather than duplicating. Rendering calls must be removed.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `YouTurnController` class tracking trigger state, turn direction, skip mode, and the in-progress waypoint list.\n- `YouTurnController.evaluate(vehicle_state, boundary, track)` returns `YouTurnDecision` (trigger/don not trigger, direction, computed path).\n- `TurnPathBuilder.build_dubins_turn(start, goal, radius)` delegates to the Core `DubinsPathSelector` from Issue #4.\n- `SkipMode` as `enum.Enum` (`Normal`, `Alternative`, `IgnoreWorkedTracks`).\n- No OpenGL calls; path returned as `list[GeoCoordDir]`.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] U-turn trigger fires when vehicle enters headland turn area.\n- [ ] Dubins path waypoints are generated correctly for both left and right turns.\n- [ ] `SkipMode` correctly controls which rows to target after the turn.\n- [ ] `CDubins` in GPS project replaced by delegation to Core `DubinsPathSelector`.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests for turn triggering, direction selection, and Dubins path generation.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives), Issue #4 (Dubins Path — Core), Issue #11 (Guidance Algorithms).\n\n## Notes\n- The `is_out_same_curve` flag decides whether the vehicle continues on the same line or advances to the next after the turn — this must be preserved.\n- `uTurnSmoothing` parameter controls waypoint density on the generated Dubins path arc."
}'
