gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Boundary and Field-Geometry Classes (CBoundary, CBoundaryList, BoundaryBuilder, CFence)",
  "labels": ["migration","core","data"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`CBoundary` manages a list of `CBoundaryList` rings. Each ring has a `turn_line` (list of `vec3` points), an `is_drive_thru` flag, and a precomputed interior polygon used for headland detection. `BoundaryBuilder` records boundary points from GPS while the vehicle drives the boundary and closes the polygon. `CFence`/`CFenceLine` manage fence lines (secondary boundaries used for obstacle avoidance). `CBoundary.IsPointInsideTurnArea` uses the ray-casting polygon test to determine if a vehicle position is inside the headland turn area for any boundary ring. The class also supports headland polygon shrinking (offsetting inward by a configured distance).\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CBoundary.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CBoundaryList.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/BoundaryBuilder.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CFence.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CFenceLine.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nAll boundary ring management, point-in-polygon tests, headland polygon construction, boundary recording, and fence-line logic must be converted without UI or OpenGL coupling.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `BoundaryRing` dataclass with `turn_line: list[GeoCoord]`, `is_drive_thru: bool`, and `headland_polygon: list[GeoCoord] | None`.\n- `BoundaryManager` class with `rings: list[BoundaryRing]`, `is_point_in_turn_area(pt: GeoCoord) -> int` (returns ring index or -1).\n- `BoundaryBuilder` as a stateful class: `start_recording()`, `add_point(coord)`, `close_boundary() -> BoundaryRing`.\n- `is_point_in_polygon(polygon, point)` as a reusable pure function using ray-casting.\n- Fence lines as `FenceLine` dataclass with a `list[GeoCoord]`.\n- No rendering calls; no `FormGPS` reference.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `is_point_in_polygon` correctly classifies points inside and outside a convex polygon.\n- [ ] `is_point_in_polygon` correctly classifies points inside and outside a concave polygon.\n- [ ] `BoundaryManager.is_point_in_turn_area` returns -1 for points outside all boundaries.\n- [ ] `BoundaryBuilder` produces a closed polygon with first point == last point.\n- [ ] `is_drive_thru` ring is ignored in `is_point_in_turn_area`.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests for polygon containment and boundary recording.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives), Issue #3 (GeoPolygon).\n\n## Notes\n- The ray-casting algorithm in the C# code uses `easting` as the X axis and `northing` as the Y axis — ensure coordinate axis order is consistent.\n- The headland inward offset (shrink) uses a constant configured via settings — inject this as a constructor parameter."
}'
