gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Section Control and Implement Management (CSection, CTool, CPatches)",
  "labels": ["migration","core"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`CSection` models one implement section: it has `is_section_on`, `is_section_required_on`, timing counters (`section_on_timer`, `section_off_timer`), left/right position offsets (in metres from centre), and a `section_btn_state` enum (`Off`, `Auto`, `On`). `CTool` manages the full array of sections: applies boundary/headland rules, handles master on/off, and sends section state byte arrays to the hardware module via `CModuleComm`. `CPatches` manages the covered-area triangle strips: each time a section moves, a new triangle strip quad is computed and added to the rendered patch list. The render list is OpenGL vertex data. `CSection` also tracks whether mapping is active for that section.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CSection.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CTool.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CPatches.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\n`CSection` state model, `CTool` section orchestration logic (boundary checks, master enable/disable, hardware byte-array construction), and `CPatches` quad-strip area accumulation must all be converted. OpenGL rendering calls in `CPatches` must be removed — the patch data structure must remain so a separate rendering module can consume it.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `SectionState` dataclass per section: `is_on`, `is_required_on`, `on_timer`, `off_timer`, `position_left`, `position_right`, `width`, `btn_state`, `is_mapping_on`.\n- `SectionBtnState` as `enum.Enum` (`OFF`, `AUTO`, `ON`).\n- `SectionController` class managing a `list[SectionState]` with `apply_boundary_rules(vehicle_pos, boundary_manager)`, `build_hardware_bytes() -> bytes`.\n- `WorkedAreaAccumulator` (replaces `CPatches`): `add_swath(left_pts, right_pts)` appends a `QuadStrip` to an in-memory list for later rendering.\n- No OpenGL calls; no `FormGPS` reference.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `SectionController.build_hardware_bytes` produces the correct 9-byte section-state packet format.\n- [ ] Section turns on when required and boundary rules allow.\n- [ ] `WorkedAreaAccumulator.add_swath` accumulates quad strips correctly.\n- [ ] `SectionBtnState` transitions (manual off → auto → manual on) work correctly.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests for byte-array construction and section state transitions.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives), Issue #2 (Field Models), Issue #13 (Boundary Management).\n\n## Notes\n- The 9-byte hardware packet format (`ss` array in C#) must match the AgOpenGPS UDP PGN protocol exactly — this is a hardware interface contract.\n- `CPatches` triangle strips are 24-byte quads in OpenGL format; the Python replacement should store as `list[tuple[GeoCoord, GeoCoord, GeoCoord, GeoCoord]]` for renderer consumption."
