gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] GPS Project File I/O Layer (BoundaryFiles, TrackFiles, ContourFiles, and Related)",
  "labels": ["migration","data"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\nThe `GPS/IO` namespace contains static file-reader/writer classes for every field data component persisted by the GPS application. These are distinct from the Core streamers (Issue #5) — they operate on the GPS-project-specific data types (`CBoundaryList`, `CTrk`, etc.) and use slightly different file formats. `BoundaryFiles.Load` is legacy-tolerant (handles duplicate `True`/`False` lines). `TrackFiles.Load` requires a `$` header and throws `InvalidDataException` on malformed content. `ContourFiles`, `HeadlandFiles`, `SectionFiles`, `FlagFiles`, `RecPathFiles`, `TramFiles`, `ElevationFiles` follow similar patterns. `FileIOUtils` provides shared path helpers.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/BoundaryFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/TrackFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/ContourFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/HeadlandFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/HeadlinesFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/SectionFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/FlagFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/RecPathFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/TramFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/Elevation.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/FieldPlaneFiles.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/IO/FileIOUtils.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nEach static class becomes a Python module with `load(field_dir: Path) -> T` and `save(data: T, field_dir: Path) -> None` functions. Legacy tolerance in `BoundaryFiles` must be preserved. `TrackFiles` strict header validation must be preserved. All `InvariantCulture` parsing replaces with Python `float(value)` (which is locale-independent).\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- Each file type in its own module: `agopengps/gps/io/boundary_files.py`, `track_files.py`, etc.\n- `load` returns `None` (not empty list) when file does not exist.\n- `save` uses atomic write (`.tmp` rename) in all cases.\n- `BoundaryFiles.load` must handle the legacy duplicate-flag format without crashing.\n- `TrackFiles.load` must raise `ValueError` (not `InvalidDataException`) for malformed content.\n- Python `float()` for all floating-point parsing — no explicit locale setting needed.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `BoundaryFiles.load` succeeds on both legacy and normal boundary files.\n- [ ] `TrackFiles.load` raises `ValueError` on missing `$` header.\n- [ ] All loaders return `None` for missing files.\n- [ ] All savers write atomically.\n- [ ] Round-trip tests: `save(load(dir))` produces identical file content.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests using `tmp_path` fixture with sample file content.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives), Issue #2 (Field Models), Issue #3 (GeoPath).\n\n## Notes\n- The GPS IO layer is separate from the Core streamer layer (Issue #5) — they may eventually be unified but keep them separate during migration to match the C# project structure.\n- `Elevation.cs` loads/saves elevation data for terrain visualisation — treat as a low-priority item within this issue."
}'
