  "title": "[Migration] AgIO UDP/Serial Communication Bridge",
  "labels": ["migration","api"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`AgIO` is a standalone Windows Forms application that acts as a communication bridge between the GPS module (serial/NTRIP) and the AgOpenGPS main application (UDP). `FormLoop` is its main loop: it manages a UDP socket (port 9999/8888), a serial port for GPS NMEA input, and separate serial passes for RTCM/NTRIP corrections. It handles PGN-format UDP messages to/from the steer, machine, and IMU modules. Key responsibilities: GPS serial receive → parse NMEA → forward via UDP; NTRIP RTCM receive → forward to GPS serial or UDP; handle `Hello` PGN handshakes; display connection status. The ISOBUS task controller is launched as an embedded form.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Forms/FormLoop.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Forms/FormUDP.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Forms/FormGPSData.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Forms/FormSource.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Forms/FormISOBUS.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Forms/FormSerialPass.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Classes/CGLM.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Properties/Settings.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Program.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nThe core bridge logic must be reimplemented as an async Python service with no Windows Forms dependency. GPS serial receive, NMEA forwarding via UDP, NTRIP RTCM forwarding, PGN Hello handshakes, and connection status tracking must all be preserved. The ISOBUS task controller is a separate concern (Issue #18).\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `AgIoBridge` as an `asyncio`-based service class in `agopengps/agio/bridge.py`.\n- `asyncio.DatagramProtocol` for UDP send/receive.\n- `pyserial-asyncio` for async serial port access.\n- Configuration via a `AgIoConfig` dataclass (subnet, ports, serial settings) injected at construction.\n- `AgIoBridge.start() -> None` launches all async tasks; `stop() -> None` cancels cleanly.\n- `on_status_change: Callable[[ConnectionStatus], None]` callback for monitoring.\n- `ConnectionStatus` dataclass tracking GPS, steer, machine, IMU connection state.\n- Logging via the module in Issue #8.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] GPS NMEA sentences received on serial port are forwarded via UDP broadcast.\n- [ ] NTRIP RTCM bytes received are forwarded to GPS serial port.\n- [ ] Hello PGN handshakes from steer/machine/IMU modules are detected and `ConnectionStatus` updated.\n- [ ] `AgIoBridge.stop()` cleanly cancels all tasks and closes sockets/serial ports.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] Integration tests using mock serial and UDP sockets.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #8 (Logging), Issue #9 (NMEA Parser), Issue #19 (PGN Protocol).\n\n## Notes\n- Windows Forms (`InitializeComponent`, `Timer`, `PerformClick`, etc.) must be entirely removed — replace with `asyncio` event loops and callbacks.\n- The UDP subnet is configurable (default 192.168.5.*) — inject via config, do not hardcode.\n- `packetSizeNTRIP` (default 256) for chunked RTCM serial forwarding — keep configurable."
}'
