gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] NTRIP RTCM Correction Client (AgIO/FormNtrip)",
  "labels": ["migration","api"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`FormNtrip` in AgIO manages the NTRIP client that streams RTCM differential correction data from a caster. It supports both TCP and HTTP/1.0 and HTTP/1.1 transport, configures the caster URL/IP, port, mount point, username, and password. It periodically sends GGA sentences to the caster (at a configurable interval) either using the current GPS fix or a manual lat/lon. It can forward received RTCM to the GPS serial port, a UDP port, or both. It tracks connection state and logs events. The caster source table can be fetched and displayed. The form embeds a `BackgroundWorker` for the connection loop.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Forms/FormNtrip.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgIO/Source/Forms/NTRIPComm.Designer.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nThe full NTRIP client loop: HTTP/TCP connection to the caster, authentication, mount-point selection, GGA-send interval, and RTCM byte forwarding. All Windows Forms UI removed and replaced with a headless async service.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `NtripClient` as an `asyncio`-based class in `agopengps/agio/ntrip_client.py`.\n- `NtripConfig` frozen dataclass: `caster_url`, `caster_port`, `mount_point`, `username`, `password`, `gga_interval_s`, `use_tcp`, `http_version`.\n- `NtripClient.start(config: NtripConfig)` opens the connection; `stop()` closes cleanly.\n- Sends GGA sentence to caster every `gga_interval_s` seconds using `on_get_gga: Callable[[], str]` callback.\n- Received RTCM bytes forwarded via `on_rtcm_received: Callable[[bytes], None]` callback.\n- `get_source_table(config: NtripConfig) -> list[str]` as an async one-shot method.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Connects to a NTRIP caster using HTTP/1.0 or HTTP/1.1 as configured.\n- [ ] Authenticates with Base64-encoded `username:password`.\n- [ ] Sends GGA sentences at the configured interval.\n- [ ] RTCM bytes delivered to the `on_rtcm_received` callback.\n- [ ] `stop()` closes the connection without error.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests with mock caster using `asyncio` test patterns.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #16 (AgIO Bridge — NTRIP bytes forwarded via bridge callbacks).\n\n## Notes\n- NTRIP protocol uses plain HTTP with `GET /<mount>` and `Authorization: Basic <base64>` — do not use standard HTTP client libraries that follow HTTP/1.1 redirects; raw TCP sockets may be needed for NTRIP/2.0.\n- The manual lat/lon override for GGA must be supported when the GPS fix is not yet available."
