gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] ISOBUS / ISO 11783 Task File Protocol (GPS/Protocols/ISOBUS/)",
  "labels": ["migration","api"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`ISO11783_TaskFile.cs` parses ISO XML task files (ISOXML) to import field boundaries and guidance tracks from third-party farm management software. `IsoXmlFieldImporter` drives the import: it reads `TASKDATA.XML`, extracts `PFD` (partfield) elements for boundary polygons, and converts them to AgOpenGPS field format. `IsoXmlParserHelpers` provides helper methods for coordinate parsing (DDI-coded lat/lon as integer millionths of a degree). `CurveCABTools` post-processes imported curve tracks. `CISOBUS.cs` in the GPS project manages the ISOBUS Task Controller communication at runtime (virtual terminal, working set, task state machine).\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Protocols/ISOBUS/ISO11783_TaskFile.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Protocols/ISOBUS/IsoXmlFieldImporter.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Protocols/ISOBUS/IsoXmlParserHelpers.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Protocols/ISOBUS/CurveCABTools.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CISOBUS.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nISO XML task file parsing, partfield boundary extraction, coordinate conversion, and curve track post-processing must be converted. The runtime ISOBUS task controller state machine in `CISOBUS` must be separated from its `FormGPS` coupling.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `IsoXmlImporter` class in `agopengps/gps/protocols/isobus/importer.py` using `xml.etree.ElementTree`.\n- `import_field(task_data_path: Path) -> list[ImportedField]` returns parsed boundary polygons as `list[GeoCoord]`.\n- `ImportedField` dataclass with `name`, `boundary_polygon`, `guidance_tracks`.\n- Coordinate parsing: ISO DDI integer millionths of degree → `Wgs84` (divide by 10^7).\n- `IsobusCommunication` class for task-controller runtime state machine (separate from importer).\n- No Windows Forms; no `FormGPS` reference.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `import_field` correctly parses a sample `TASKDATA.XML` with one partfield.\n- [ ] DDI integer coordinates converted to `Wgs84` with sub-metre accuracy.\n- [ ] Malformed XML raises `ValueError` with a descriptive message.\n- [ ] `IsobusCommunication` state machine transitions correctly through task states.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests with sample ISOXML fixture files.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives — Wgs84, GeoCoord).\n\n## Notes\n- ISO 11783 Part 10 (Task Data) uses integer coordinates as millionths of a degree — do not use floating-point intermediate representations for the conversion.\n- The AgIO ISOBUS form (`FormISOBUS`) wraps the CAN-over-UDP task controller — consider using `can` or `python-can` library for future CAN integration."
