gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] PGN Protocol Layer and Module Communication (Pgns, CModuleComm, AgDiag)",
  "labels": ["migration","api"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\nAgOpenGPS uses a custom binary protocol over UDP called PGN (Parameter Group Number, borrowed from NMEA 2000 concepts). `Pgns` in `AgDiag/Protocol` defines the byte-level structures: each PGN message is a fixed-length byte array with a `0x80, 0x81, 0x7F, <pgn_id>` preamble. `PgnBase` provides `get_byte`, `get_int` (little-endian two-byte), `is_bit_on`, `set_bytes_from_message`, and `to_hex_string`. Concrete PGNs include `CPGN_FE` (autosteer data: speed, status, steer angle, sections), `CPGN_FD` (autosteer module config), `CPGN_FC` (autosteer settings), `CPGN_FB` (autosteer config). `CModuleComm` in the GPS project builds and parses these packets, manages the work-switch and steer-switch logic, and sends section-state bytes to the steer module.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgDiag/Protocol/Pgns.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgDiag/Protocol/UdpCommunication.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS/Classes/CModuleComm.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nAll PGN byte-level message structures, the UDP receive loop, and the module communication manager must be converted. The `UdpCommunication` async receive loop uses `Task.Factory.StartNew` with `CancellationToken` — replace with `asyncio`.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `PgnBase` Python class with `get_byte(index) -> int`, `get_int(lo, hi) -> int` (little-endian), `is_bit_on(byte_idx, bit) -> bool`, `set_bytes_from_message(data: bytes)`, `to_hex_string() -> str`.\n- Each concrete PGN as a subclass of `PgnBase` with typed property accessors.\n- `PgnMessage` dataclass with preamble validation (`bytes[0:2] == [0x80, 0x81]`).\n- `ModuleCommunication` class in `agopengps/gps/module_comm.py` with `build_section_bytes(sections: list[SectionState]) -> bytes`, `parse_steer_data(data: bytes) -> SteerData`, `check_work_switch(state)`, `check_steer_switch(state)`.\n- Async UDP receive loop using `asyncio.DatagramProtocol`.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `PgnBase.get_int` correctly assembles little-endian two-byte integers.\n- [ ] `CPGN_FE` extracts speed, status, steer angle, and section bits correctly from a sample byte array.\n- [ ] `ModuleCommunication.build_section_bytes` produces the correct 9-byte packet for a known section configuration.\n- [ ] UDP receive loop dispatches incoming bytes to the correct PGN handler.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests with hardcoded byte arrays for each PGN type.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #14 (Section Control — `SectionState` used in `build_section_bytes`).\n\n## Notes\n- PGN preamble is always `[0x80, 0x81, 0x7F, <pgn_id>]` — validate on receive, discard invalid frames.\n- The PGN protocol is a hardware interface contract — byte offsets must match exactly.\n- `to_hex_string` format: `AA-BB-CC-...` (hyphen-separated hex bytes, matching `BitConverter.ToString` in C#)."
}'
