gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] GPS Output — NMEA Sentence Builders (GPS_Out PGN_GGA, PGN_RMC, PGN_VTG, PGN_GSA)",
  "labels": ["migration","api"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`GPS_Out` is a standalone utility application that re-transmits GPS data received from AgIO/AOG in NMEA sentence format over UDP or serial. It receives position data (lat, lon, altitude, speed, heading, fix quality, satellites, HDOP, age) from AgIO and AOG via UDP, then builds and transmits `$GP(GGA|RMC|VTG|GSA)` sentences with correct NMEA checksums. `PGN_GGA` builds the GGA sentence with UTC time, lat/lon in DDM format, fix quality, satellite count, HDOP, altitude. `PGN_RMC` adds speed-over-ground and course-over-ground. `PGN_VTG` adds the VTG speed/course sentence. `UDPComm` handles the two UDP sockets (receive from AgIO, send formatted NMEA).\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/GPS_Out/Source/PGNs/PGN_GGA.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS_Out/Source/PGNs/PGN_RMC.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS_Out/Source/PGNs/PGN_VTG.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS_Out/Source/PGNs/PGN_GSA.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS_Out/Source/Classes/UDPcomm.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS_Out/Source/Classes/SerialSend.cs`\n- `SourceCode/GPS_Out/Source/Classes/clsTools.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nAll four NMEA sentence builders, the NMEA checksum function, and the UDP/serial output must be converted without Windows Forms dependency.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `NmeaBuilder` class in `agopengps/gps_out/nmea_builder.py` with `build_gga(fix_data) -> str`, `build_rmc(fix_data) -> str`, `build_vtg(fix_data) -> str`, `build_gsa(fix_data) -> str`.\n- `GpsFixData` frozen dataclass: `latitude`, `longitude`, `altitude`, `speed_knots`, `heading`, `fix_quality`, `satellites`, `hdop`, `age`.\n- `nmea_checksum(sentence: str) -> str` computes XOR checksum between `$` and `*`.\n- `GpsOutService` async class that receives fix data via callback and transmits NMEA sentences on a configurable interval.\n- `sentence_prefix` configurable (`$GP` or `$GN`).\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `build_gga` produces a valid GGA sentence for a known input, matching C# output character-for-character.\n- [ ] `nmea_checksum` matches the C# `CheckSum` function for all sentence types.\n- [ ] Lat/lon formatted as DDM (degrees + decimal minutes) with correct hemisphere letters.\n- [ ] UTC time formatted as `HHmmss.ff`.\n- [ ] All public functions have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests comparing builder output to known NMEA reference sentences.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #1 (Geospatial Primitives — Wgs84 for coordinate input).\n\n## Notes\n- NMEA lat/lon in DDM format: degrees (integer) + decimal minutes (float) — not decimal degrees. Be precise about the conversion.\n- The `$` prefix and sentence type (`GP`/`GN`) are configurable in `Properties.Settings.Default.SentenceStart`.\n- `PGN_GGA` in GPS_Out is entirely different from PGN packets in the module communication protocol — name carefully to avoid confusion."
}'
