gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Application Architecture — Presenter/ViewModel Pattern (ApplicationCore, ApplicationPresenter, ViewModels)",
  "labels": ["migration","core"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\n`ApplicationCore` is the composition root for the WPF application layer: it wires together `ApplicationModel` (domain state: fields directory, vehicles directory, current lat/lon, heading, local plane), `FieldStreamer`, `FieldDescriptionStreamer`, `ApplicationPresenter`, and `ApplicationViewModel`. The presenter/view-model pattern (MVP + MVVM hybrid) uses `IApplicationPresenter`, `IErrorPresenter`, `IPanelPresenter`, `ISelectFieldPanelPresenter`, `IConfigMenuPanelPresenter` interfaces. `ApplicationViewModel` extends `DayNightAndUnitsViewModel` which provides unit conversion (metric/imperial), day/night mode, and observable property change notifications (`INotifyPropertyChanged`). `RelayCommand` wraps actions as `ICommand`. `SelectFieldViewModel` and `ConfigMenuViewModel` handle field selection and configuration menus.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/ApplicationCore.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Models/ApplicationModel.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Presenters/ApplicationPresenter.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Presenters/FieldStreamerPresenter.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/ViewModels/ApplicationViewModel.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/ViewModels/ViewModel.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/ViewModels/RelayCommand.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/ViewModels/SelectFieldViewModels/SelectFieldViewModel.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/ViewModels/SelectFieldViewModels/FieldTableViewModel.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/ViewModels/Configuration/ConfigViewModel.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/ViewModels/Base/DayNightAndUnitsViewModel.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core/Interfaces/Presenters/*.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nThe composition root, domain model, and presenter interfaces must be refactored for a Python service-oriented architecture. `INotifyPropertyChanged` (WPF-specific) must be replaced with Python observable patterns. `ICommand`/`RelayCommand` must be replaced with plain callables or `asyncio` coroutines.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- `ApplicationCore` Python class as a simple composition root: constructs and wires `ApplicationModel`, `FieldStreamer`, `ApplicationPresenter`.\n- `ApplicationModel` as a plain dataclass with `fields_dir`, `vehicles_dir`, `current_lat_lon`, `heading`, `local_plane`.\n- Presenter interfaces replaced by Python Protocol classes (structural subtyping).\n- Observable property changes via a simple `Observable` mixin using `dataclasses.field` and callbacks (`on_change: Callable`).\n- `DayNightAndUnitsViewModel` units logic (metric/imperial conversion) as a standalone utility class.\n- `SelectFieldViewModel` commands as plain methods that the UI layer calls directly.\n- No WPF, no `INotifyPropertyChanged`, no `ICommand`.\n- Full type hints.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `ApplicationCore` correctly wires all dependencies.\n- [ ] `ApplicationModel` holds correct directory paths derived from a base `pathlib.Path`.\n- [ ] Presenter interfaces defined as `typing.Protocol` classes.\n- [ ] `SelectFieldViewModel.delete_field` removes the field from the model and filesystem.\n- [ ] Unit conversion (metric ↔ imperial) is tested.\n- [ ] All public members have type hints.\n- [ ] pytest tests for composition root, field selection, and unit conversion.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- Issue #2 (Field Models), Issue #5 (Field Streamers).\n\n## Notes\n- WPF data binding (`INotifyPropertyChanged`) has no direct Python equivalent — for a headless service or CLI, plain callbacks are sufficient; for a future GUI (e.g., PyQt), use `pyqtSignal`.\n- `RelayCommand` wrapping `ICommand` is WPF-specific — not needed in Python."
}'
