gh_api '{
  "title": "[Migration] Test Suite Migration — pytest Equivalents for All Existing C# Tests",
  "labels": ["migration","testing"],
  "body": "## Code Review Summary\nThe C# solution contains three test projects. `AgOpenGPS.Core.Tests` has NUnit tests for all geospatial primitive types (`GeoCoordTests`, `Wgs84Tests`, `GeoLineSegmentTests`, `GeoPolygonTests`, `GeoBoundingBoxTests`). `AgLibrary.Tests` has tests for `XmlSettingsHandler` covering all supported field types. `AgOpenGPS.Tests` is the integration test project (currently minimal). Tests use NUnit `Assert.That` with `Is.EqualTo`, `Is.GreaterThan`, `Is.LessThan` matchers. All test inputs are numeric with known mathematical answers. The WGS84 test includes regional (Amsterdam to Den Dungen, ~85 km) and antipodal (20 000+ km) distance checks.\n\n## Source Files\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core.Tests/Models/Base/GeoCoordTests.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core.Tests/Models/Base/Wgs84Tests.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core.Tests/Models/Base/GeoLineSegmentTests.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core.Tests/Models/Base/GeoPolygonTests.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgOpenGPS.Core.Tests/Models/Base/GeoBoundingBoxTests.cs`\n- `SourceCode/AgLibrary.Tests/Settings/XmlSettingsHandlerTests.cs`\n\n## What Must Be Converted\nEvery NUnit test case must have a direct pytest equivalent. The `TestSettings` helper class used in `XmlSettingsHandlerTests` must be recreated as a Python dataclass/class. The `TestSettings.xml` fixture file must be recreated in the `tests/fixtures/` directory.\n\n## Python Implementation Requirements\n- All tests in `tests/` directory using pytest (no unittest).\n- `pytest.approx` for floating-point comparisons (replace `Is.EqualTo` on floats).\n- Exact integer comparisons use `assert x == y`.\n- Test fixtures using `pytest`s `tmp_path` fixture for file I/O tests.\n- `tests/fixtures/TestSettings.xml` recreated matching the C# version.\n- Test file organisation mirrors C# structure: `tests/core/models/base/test_geo_coord.py`, etc.\n- `conftest.py` at root `tests/` level for shared fixtures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All C# test cases have exact Python equivalents.\n- [ ] `Wgs84` haversine distance tests pass (Amsterdam distances, antipodal distance).\n- [ ] `GeoCoord` arithmetic tests pass (distance, min, max, average, triangle area).\n- [ ] `GeoBoundingBox` tests pass (include, is_inside, scaled).\n- [ ] `XmlSettingsHandler` round-trip tests pass.\n- [ ] All tests pass with `pytest -v`.\n- [ ] Test coverage ≥ 80% for all migrated core modules.\n- [ ] Code passes ruff linting.\n\n## Dependencies\n- All implementation issues (#1–#23) — tests should be written alongside the implementation.\n\n## Notes\n- NUnit `Assert.That(distance, Is.EqualTo(distanceBack))` → `assert distance == approx(distance_back)` with appropriate tolerance.\n- The `TestSettings.xml` fixture must be bit-for-bit compatible with the C# `XmlSettingsHandler` format to validate round-trip compatibility."
